* ==================================================================
* tb_dr0014_sampling -- THE FOUR TERMS DR-0014'S DERIVATION ASSUMES
* AWAY, each as a measured number (issue #61).
*
* GENERATED by design/adc-top/gen_adc_top.py -- do not edit.
*
* DR-0014 moves the sampling phase from the CDAC top plate to the
* bottom plates. Its charge-balance derivation shows that
* k = C_arr/(C_arr + C_par) then multiplies the sampled input and
* every DAC step alike, so it cancels from the comparator's decision
* instead of dividing the DAC step alone. That derivation is exact
* only if four things are negligible, and the record itself says so:
*
*   1. the top-plate V_cm switch's own charge injection, and its
*      side-to-side MISMATCH (the injection is claimed to be
*      signal-independent -- an offset -- which is the classic reason
*      to sample on the bottom plate, and is SHOWN here, not assumed);
*   2. the bottom-plate input switches' injection, which happens one
*      whole bit cycle AFTER the top-plate switch has opened, i.e.
*      onto a node that is already isolated;
*   3. the fourth leg's cost in bit-trial settling -- one more T-gate's
*      junction and overlap load on every bottom plate, against the
*      31.25 ns settling half of the bit cycle;
*   4. the second-order residue left by C_par MISMATCH between the two
*      sides, i.e. what survives the first-order cancellation.
*
* It also re-takes the two measurements DR-0014 invalidated the prior
* evidence for: the sampling path's own gain error and linearity
* (DR-0012/DR-0013's 0.421 LSB was measured on a dedicated top-plate
* switch that no longer exists), and the series R_on of the new input
* path -- nine parallel cell T-gates per side, not one 40u/80u switch.
*
* METHOD. One transient carries DR-0014's real two-phase schedule on
* DR-0003's 62.5 ns clock:
*   0 .. 187.5 ns      acquire: top plate held at V_cm by its own
*                     switch, every bottom plate on V_in
*   187.5 ns          THE SAMPLING INSTANT -- the top-plate switch
*                     opens and the top node floats
*   250 ns          the bottom plates leave V_in for V_cm, one
*                     whole bit cycle later
*   375 ns          one bit trial: weight 256 engaged, p side to
*                     V_REF and n side to GND (MCS, DR-0011)
*
* Nothing else moves at the sampling instant, which is what makes
* term 1 DIRECTLY measurable: the top plate sits at V_cm before that
* edge by construction, so its displacement after it IS the switch's
* injection, with no reference simulation and no subtraction of two
* large numbers. Term 2 is read the same way at the f = 0 level, where
* both sides sit at V_cm and the ideal sampled step is exactly zero.
*
* V_REF AND V_cm ARE IDEAL SOURCES HERE, deliberately, and this is the
* one place this deck differs from sim/adc-inl-dnl/. DR-0002's
* reference network is a shared node; with 18 array sides on one deck
* it would couple every branch to every other and the A/B comparisons
* below -- which are differences of two branches -- would report that
* coupling as the effect under test. Reference droop is a real term
* and it is measured, with the real network, by sim/adc-inl-dnl/ and
* sim/adc-power/; it is not double-counted here.
*
* EVERY QUANTITY IS PUBLISHED IN LSB, computed by a B-source inside
* the netlist rather than by the measure expression, because the
* harness does not expose `.param lsb` to the `.control` block and LSB
* is supply-dependent (ratiometric spec, README.md note [c]).
* ==================================================================

.param vref={vdd_val}
.param vcm={vdd_val/2}
.param lsb={vdd_val/1024}
.param ibias=10u

* ---- rails -------------------------------------------------------
vddd vddd 0 dc {vdd_val}
vddt vddt 0 dc {vdd_val}
vddc vddc 0 dc {vdd_val}
vrefs vrefn 0 dc {vref}
vcms vcmn 0 dc {vcm}
vonh onh 0 dc {vdd_val}
vonl onl 0 dc 0
* The comparator strobe is held LOW: the latch is in reset and the
* preamp is tracking, which is the state the top plate is in while a
* DAC step settles. Kickback on the strobe edge is a different
* quantity and a different deck (sim/comparator-kickback/).
vcmpstrobe cmpstrobe 0 dc 0

* ---- DR-0014's two-phase sample, as pure edges --------------------
* Each control is one clean edge from an ideal source. The controller
* that generates them from the phase ring is verified separately and
* exhaustively by sim/sar-logic-functional/ (the four-leg one-hot
* invariant and the measured samp_tp -> samp_bp lead); re-deriving
* them here would make this deck's numbers depend on that logic's
* delays instead of on the analog terms it exists to measure.
* `nrel` rises exactly as `smpbp` falls, with matched 100 ps edges --
* the delay balance design/sar-logic/ builds smpb and engnb to hold.
vsmptp smptp 0 pulse({vdd_val} 0 187.5n 100p 100p 10u 20u)
vsmpbp smpbp 0 pulse({vdd_val} 0 250n 100p 100p 10u 20u)
vnrel  nrel  0 pulse(0 {vdd_val} 250n 100p 100p 10u 20u)
* weight 256's release leg: engaged at the trial, so it is high only
* between the end of the sample and the trial edge.
vnrel256 nrel256 0 pwl(0 0 250n 0 250.1n {vdd_val} 375n {vdd_val} 375.1n 0)
vhi256 hi256 0 pulse(0 {vdd_val} 375n 100p 100p 10u 20u)
vlo256 lo256 0 pulse(0 {vdd_val} 375n 100p 100p 10u 20u)
* the settling branches never sample, so their weight-256 release leg
* is high from t = 0 until the trial edge.
vbrel brel 0 pwl(0 {vdd_val} 375n {vdd_val} 375.1n 0)

* ==================================================================
* GROUP A -- terms 1 and 2, plus the sampling path's gain and
* linearity. Five differential pairs, identical except for the input.
* ==================================================================
* ---- pair a0: differential input f = -0.900 x V_cm
va0srcp a0_srcp 0 dc {vcm*0.09999999999999998}
Ra0sp a0_srcp a0_pinp 25
Ca0xp a0_pinp 0 1n
Xa0tswp a0_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa0arrp a0_topp a0_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
va0srcn a0_srcn 0 dc {vcm*1.9}
Ra0sn a0_srcn a0_pinn 25
Ca0xn a0_pinn 0 1n
Xa0tswn a0_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa0arrn a0_topn a0_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
ia0b vddc a0_ib dc {ibias}
Xa0cmp a0_topp a0_topn cmpstrobe a0_ib a0_do a0_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(a0_do)=0 v(a0_dob)={vdd_val}
ba0dp a0_dp 0 V = (v(a0_topp)-vcm)/lsb
ba0dn a0_dn 0 V = (v(a0_topn)-vcm)/lsb
ba0dd a0_dd 0 V = (v(a0_topp)-v(a0_topn))/lsb

* ---- pair a1: differential input f = -0.450 x V_cm
va1srcp a1_srcp 0 dc {vcm*0.55}
Ra1sp a1_srcp a1_pinp 25
Ca1xp a1_pinp 0 1n
Xa1tswp a1_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa1arrp a1_topp a1_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
va1srcn a1_srcn 0 dc {vcm*1.45}
Ra1sn a1_srcn a1_pinn 25
Ca1xn a1_pinn 0 1n
Xa1tswn a1_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa1arrn a1_topn a1_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
ia1b vddc a1_ib dc {ibias}
Xa1cmp a1_topp a1_topn cmpstrobe a1_ib a1_do a1_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(a1_do)=0 v(a1_dob)={vdd_val}
ba1dp a1_dp 0 V = (v(a1_topp)-vcm)/lsb
ba1dn a1_dn 0 V = (v(a1_topn)-vcm)/lsb
ba1dd a1_dd 0 V = (v(a1_topp)-v(a1_topn))/lsb

* ---- pair a2: differential input f = +0.000 x V_cm
va2srcp a2_srcp 0 dc {vcm*1.0}
Ra2sp a2_srcp a2_pinp 25
Ca2xp a2_pinp 0 1n
Xa2tswp a2_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa2arrp a2_topp a2_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
va2srcn a2_srcn 0 dc {vcm*1.0}
Ra2sn a2_srcn a2_pinn 25
Ca2xn a2_pinn 0 1n
Xa2tswn a2_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa2arrn a2_topn a2_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
ia2b vddc a2_ib dc {ibias}
Xa2cmp a2_topp a2_topn cmpstrobe a2_ib a2_do a2_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(a2_do)=0 v(a2_dob)={vdd_val}
ba2dp a2_dp 0 V = (v(a2_topp)-vcm)/lsb
ba2dn a2_dn 0 V = (v(a2_topn)-vcm)/lsb
ba2dd a2_dd 0 V = (v(a2_topp)-v(a2_topn))/lsb

* ---- pair a3: differential input f = +0.450 x V_cm
va3srcp a3_srcp 0 dc {vcm*1.45}
Ra3sp a3_srcp a3_pinp 25
Ca3xp a3_pinp 0 1n
Xa3tswp a3_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa3arrp a3_topp a3_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
va3srcn a3_srcn 0 dc {vcm*0.55}
Ra3sn a3_srcn a3_pinn 25
Ca3xn a3_pinn 0 1n
Xa3tswn a3_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa3arrn a3_topn a3_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
ia3b vddc a3_ib dc {ibias}
Xa3cmp a3_topp a3_topn cmpstrobe a3_ib a3_do a3_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(a3_do)=0 v(a3_dob)={vdd_val}
ba3dp a3_dp 0 V = (v(a3_topp)-vcm)/lsb
ba3dn a3_dn 0 V = (v(a3_topn)-vcm)/lsb
ba3dd a3_dd 0 V = (v(a3_topp)-v(a3_topn))/lsb

* ---- pair a4: differential input f = +0.900 x V_cm
va4srcp a4_srcp 0 dc {vcm*1.9}
Ra4sp a4_srcp a4_pinp 25
Ca4xp a4_pinp 0 1n
Xa4tswp a4_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa4arrp a4_topp a4_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
va4srcn a4_srcn 0 dc {vcm*0.09999999999999998}
Ra4sn a4_srcn a4_pinn 25
Ca4xn a4_pinn 0 1n
Xa4tswn a4_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xa4arrn a4_topn a4_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
ia4b vddc a4_ib dc {ibias}
Xa4cmp a4_topp a4_topn cmpstrobe a4_ib a4_do a4_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(a4_do)=0 v(a4_dob)={vdd_val}
ba4dp a4_dp 0 V = (v(a4_topp)-vcm)/lsb
ba4dn a4_dn 0 V = (v(a4_topn)-vcm)/lsb
ba4dd a4_dd 0 V = (v(a4_topp)-v(a4_topn))/lsb

* ==================================================================
* GROUP B -- term 3. Two single sides, engaged into the same weight-
* 256 trial from the same released state, differing ONLY in whether
* the cell carries DR-0014's fourth leg. Neither samples: `smpbp` is
* not routed to them and their inputs sit at V_cm, so what is
* compared is the bit trial alone.
* ==================================================================
* b4: the DR-0014 four-leg cell, fourth leg present but off
Xb4tsw b4_top vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xb4arr b4_top vcmn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd onl brel hi256 onl onh onl onl onh
+ onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh
+ onl onl adc_cdac_side
ib4b vddc b4_ib dc {ibias}
Xb4cmp b4_top vcmn cmpstrobe b4_ib b4_do b4_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(b4_do)=0 v(b4_dob)={vdd_val}
bb4d b4_d 0 V = (v(b4_top)-vcm)/lsb

* b3: the DR-0011 three-leg cell, everything else identical
Xb3tsw b3_top vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xb3arr b3_top vrefn vcmn 0 vddd brel hi256 onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh
+ onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl onh onl onl
+ tb3_cdac_side
ib3b vddc b3_ib dc {ibias}
Xb3cmp b3_top vcmn cmpstrobe b3_ib b3_do b3_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(b3_do)=0 v(b3_dob)={vdd_val}
bb3d b3_d 0 V = (v(b3_top)-vcm)/lsb

* ==================================================================
* GROUP C -- term 4. The same pair as group A's level 3 (f = +0.450),
* with a deliberate capacitance imbalance on the p top plate. Group
* A's a3 IS the matched reference -- same input, same controls, same
* deck -- so the difference is attributable to the imbalance alone.
* ==================================================================
* ---- pair c0: differential input f = +0.450 x V_cm, +10 fF on the p top plate
vc0srcp c0_srcp 0 dc {vcm*1.45}
Rc0sp c0_srcp c0_pinp 25
Cc0xp c0_pinp 0 1n
Xc0tswp c0_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xc0arrp c0_topp c0_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
vc0srcn c0_srcn 0 dc {vcm*0.55}
Rc0sn c0_srcn c0_pinn 25
Cc0xn c0_pinn 0 1n
Xc0tswn c0_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xc0arrn c0_topn c0_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
Cc0dcpar c0_topp 0 10f
ic0b vddc c0_ib dc {ibias}
Xc0cmp c0_topp c0_topn cmpstrobe c0_ib c0_do c0_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(c0_do)=0 v(c0_dob)={vdd_val}
bc0dp c0_dp 0 V = (v(c0_topp)-vcm)/lsb
bc0dn c0_dn 0 V = (v(c0_topn)-vcm)/lsb
bc0dd c0_dd 0 V = (v(c0_topp)-v(c0_topn))/lsb

* ---- pair c1: differential input f = +0.450 x V_cm, +30 fF on the p top plate
vc1srcp c1_srcp 0 dc {vcm*1.45}
Rc1sp c1_srcp c1_pinp 25
Cc1xp c1_pinp 0 1n
Xc1tswp c1_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xc1arrp c1_topp c1_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
vc1srcn c1_srcn 0 dc {vcm*0.55}
Rc1sn c1_srcn c1_pinn 25
Cc1xn c1_pinn 0 1n
Xc1tswn c1_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xc1arrn c1_topn c1_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
Cc1dcpar c1_topp 0 30f
ic1b vddc c1_ib dc {ibias}
Xc1cmp c1_topp c1_topn cmpstrobe c1_ib c1_do c1_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(c1_do)=0 v(c1_dob)={vdd_val}
bc1dp c1_dp 0 V = (v(c1_topp)-vcm)/lsb
bc1dn c1_dn 0 V = (v(c1_topn)-vcm)/lsb
bc1dd c1_dd 0 V = (v(c1_topp)-v(c1_topn))/lsb

* ---- pair c2: differential input f = +0.450 x V_cm, +100 fF on the p top plate
vc2srcp c2_srcp 0 dc {vcm*1.45}
Rc2sp c2_srcp c2_pinp 25
Cc2xp c2_pinp 0 1n
Xc2tswp c2_topp vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xc2arrp c2_topp c2_pinp vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 hi256 onl nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
vc2srcn c2_srcn 0 dc {vcm*0.55}
Rc2sn c2_srcn c2_pinn 25
Cc2xn c2_pinn 0 1n
Xc2tswn c2_topn vcmn smptp vddt 0 adc_tp_sw
Xc2arrn c2_topn c2_pinn vrefn vcmn 0 vddd smpbp nrel256 onl lo256 nrel onl
+ onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl nrel onl onl
+ nrel onl onl nrel onl onl adc_cdac_side
Cc2dcpar c2_topp 0 100f
ic2b vddc c2_ib dc {ibias}
Xc2cmp c2_topp c2_topn cmpstrobe c2_ib c2_do c2_dob vddc 0 comparator
.nodeset v(c2_do)=0 v(c2_dob)={vdd_val}
